            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Dead Letter Queue Growth\n**WHAT:** Dead Letter Queue Growth: dlq_depth signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `messaging-platform` (messaging / queue, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Dead-lettered messages are business events that were permanently lost; the threshold reflects the manual replay capacity of one engineer.\n\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-dlq-growth.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-clear-dlq` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `messaging-platform.prod.messaging-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-messaging-delivery` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Dead Letter Queue Growth — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-dlq-growth.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Dead Letter Queue Growth — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-dlq-growth.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Dead Letter Queue Growth\n{{value}} returned to n