            "locked": false,
            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P3 · Consumer Lag Exhaustion Forecast\n**WHAT:** Backlogs are the textbook forecastable failure: growth is monotonic and the drain rate is measurable, so exhaustion time is computable hours ahead of impact.\n\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `messaging-platform` (messaging / queue, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Nothing is broken yet. A boundary will be crossed if nobody acts within the lead time this monitor provides.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Extrapolating the recent trend, this resource is projected to cross its limit inside the forecast horizon. It has not crossed it yet — that is the point.\n**OWNER:** cloud-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-lag-forecast.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `remediate-scale-workload` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `messaging-platform.prod.messaging-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-messaging-delivery` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Consumer Lag Exhaustion Forecast — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P3. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-lag-forecast.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Consumer Lag Exhaustion Forecast — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/consumer-lag-forecast.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recovery}}\n## Recovered · Consumer Lag Exhaustion Forecast\n{{value}} returned to normal. Error-budget impact recorded against `slo-messaging-delivery`. No action required; the correlation group closes when every child recovers.\n{{/is_recovery}}\n{{#is_warning_recovery}}\nWarning cleared for {{value}}.\n{{/is_warning_recovery}}",
