            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · vSphere Cluster HA Capacity Degraded\n**WHAT:** vSphere Cluster HA Capacity Degraded: availability signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `virtualization-platform` (vmware / vsphere_cluster, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Failover capacity below one host means the cluster can no longer survive a host loss — an HA design contract, not a baseline.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-cluster-ha-degraded.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-vmware` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `vmware-cluster.prod.virtualization-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-vmware-cluster-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## vSphere Cluster HA Capacity Degraded — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-cluster-ha-degraded.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## vSphere Cluster HA Capacity Degraded — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-cluster-ha-degraded.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\