            "message": "{{#is_alert}}\n## P2 · Memory Ballooning / Swapping On Host\n**WHAT:** Memory Ballooning / Swapping On Host: saturation signal detected by threshold analysis.\n**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`\n**SERVICE:** `virtualization-platform` (vmware / esxi_host, tier0)\n**BUSINESS IMPACT:** The service still functions but measurably worse; a subset of traffic or users is failing.\n**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Any host-level swap-in means the hypervisor is overcommitted past what the guests can absorb; the boundary is zero by design.\n\n**OWNER:** infrastructure-engineering · support 24x7 · this does not page\n**DO THIS NEXT:** Open the runbook, confirm scope from the group tags, and follow the validation steps. The attached workflow output already contains the standard diagnostics.\n**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-memory-ballooning.md\n**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `diag-vmware` has run; its output is attached to this event.\n**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `virtualization.prod.virtualization-platform` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.\n**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-vmware-cluster-availability` · this condition consumes error budget\n{{/is_alert}}\n{{#is_warning}}\n## Memory Ballooning / Swapping On Host — warning\nApproaching the alert condition on {{value}}. Investigate before it becomes P2. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-memory-ballooning.md\n{{/is_warning}}\n{{#is_no_data}}\n## Memory Ballooning / Swapping On Host — NO DATA\nTelemetry stopped arriving for {{value}}. Treat this as a telemetry-health incident: an unmonitored resource is worse than an alerting one. Runbook: https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/vmware-memory-ballooning.md\n{{/is_no_data}}\n{{#is_recover